 ## References
 
 Core definitions live in `include/pypto/core/common.h` and `include/pypto/ir/`; registry and type-inference implementations are in `src/ir/`, with operator implementations grouped under `src/ir/op/{tensor_ops,tile_ops,sync_ops}/`.
+
+
+### Explicit-stride in-core tensor views
+
+`pl.tensor.view(root, shape, strides=...)` can describe positive, non-overlapping
+ND rows over a packed, fully valid local GM Tensor without allocating or copying.
+The result shares the original MemRef. This initial form requires a fully valid
+target, excludes sub-byte FP4 and distributed tensors, and is rejected in
+orchestration rather than converted to a runtime reshape. Static address spans
+are checked against source capacity; with symbolic extents the caller must ensure
+positive strides and an in-bounds final element before using the alias. Native
+cache bindings must retain their page-width/capacity checks. Normal root Tensor
+contiguity checks and ordinary shape-only view rules are unchanged.
+
+For example, a contiguous `[P,page_bytes]` INT8 cache can expose `[P,32,128]`
+with strides `[page_bytes,128,1]`, skipping each page's scale bytes. The compiler
+does not load the scale region or make a compact copy. This metadata capability
+alone does not prove multi-ND device correctness or full-operator speedup.
